<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shin Chapata</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chapata</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shin Chapata was a Buddhist monk of the Pagan Kingdom who was ordained in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahavihara">Mahavihara</a> tradition and returned to Pagan around 1190 with four other monks. With the support of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narapatisithu">Narapatisithu</a> they founded a Sinhalese order of monks, which divided the Burmese sangha but strengthened links with Sri Lankan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theravada-buddhism">Theravada Buddhism</a>. The Chapata pagoda at Pagan is attributed to him.</p></div>
